Example 2

Real-Time Use Case (Logging Agent)

Here’s a more practical example (Fluentd logging DaemonSet) 👇

apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: DaemonSet
metadata:
  name: fluentd-daemonset
  namespace: kube-system
spec:
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: fluentd

  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: fluentd
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: fluentd
        image: fluent/fluentd:v1.16
        volumeMounts:
        - name: varlog
          mountPath: /var/log

      volumes:
      - name: varlog
        hostPath:
          path: /var/log



Key Sections Explained

kind: DaemonSet → Ensures 1 pod per node

selector → Matches pods

template → Pod definition

tolerations → Run on master nodes

nodeSelector → Target specific nodes

volumes (hostPath) → Access node files



commands 



1. Create DaemonSet

kubectl apply -f daemonset.yaml

2. Check DaemonSet

kubectl get daemonsets

kubectl get ds


3. Check Pods (per node)

kubectl get pods -o wide


4. Describe DaemonSet

kubectl describe ds nginx-daemon


5. Delete DaemonSet

kubectl delete ds nginx-daemon